{"repositoryId":1376665628,"availability":"available","full":"abramsluka/atlas","name":"atlas","description":"Personal health OS with an AI coach across training, sleep, nutrition and journaling. Next.js 16, Supabase, Claude.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-19T03:09:28Z","updated":"2026-10-16T03:52:22Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://atlas-phi-plum.vercel.app","topics":["ai","health","nextjs","pwa","supabase","tanstack-query","typescript"],"demo":"https://atlas-phi-plum.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T11:32:10.097Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T11:32:10.097Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T11:32:10.097Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T11:32:10.097Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A personal life-operating-system built around the idea that the data you already generate every day should actually tell you something. Atlas pulls together training, sleep, nutrition, body composition and journaling into one dashboard, and then runs an AI coach across all of it that can answer questions like \"why has my recovery been bad this week\" using the actual numbers instead of generic advice.","Think of it as what a Whoop or Oura app would look like if it had Claude sitting behind it with access to everything, rather than a recovery score and a paragraph of boilerplate.","Status: live in production and in daily use. Invite-only for a small group of family and friends, so there is no public signup."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abramsluka/atlas/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"74cab8701b7b8c46ae354b429d4b1510be213d108d6a4895f6ccf365f21e37b5","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T11:32:10.178Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T11:32:10.178Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A personal life-operating-system built around the idea that the data you already gener